Subject: gfx_opengl: read the screen back as RGBA on ES, and pack it down

Audit patch P4 (docs/substrate-audit.md 1.4).

`glReadPixels(..., GL_RGB, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, ...)` is not legal in OpenGL ES
3.0: the only formats guaranteed for the default framebuffer are
GL_RGBA/GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE and the implementation-preferred pair queried through
GL_IMPLEMENTATION_COLOR_READ_FORMAT/TYPE. ANGLE-Metal takes the spec at its
word and returns GL_INVALID_OPERATION, which this function detects and reports
as a clean failure - so F12 takes no screenshot, and neither does
`--screenshot-frame`, which is the seeded replay's evidence (M-001).

The read therefore goes into a scratch RGBA buffer under gl_es and is packed
to RGB for the caller, which is unchanged. The desktop path is untouched, so
the oracle's screenshots are still the same bytes as before.

diff --git a/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp b/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
index 7ca66e188..8349def05 100644
--- a/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
+++ b/port/fast3d/gfx_opengl.cpp
@@ -2783,9 +2783,33 @@ static bool gfx_opengl_read_screen_pixels(int x, int y, int width, int height, v
         // drain anything that was already pending, so the check below is ours
     }
 
-    glReadPixels(x, y, width, height, GL_RGB, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, rgb);
+    bool ok;
 
-    const bool ok = (glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR);
+    if (gl_es) {
+        // GL_RGB is not a legal glReadPixels format in ES 3.0 - only
+        // GL_RGBA/GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE plus the one pair the implementation
+        // advertises are guaranteed - so the read goes into a scratch RGBA
+        // buffer and is packed down to the RGB the caller asked for. Without
+        // this the read fails cleanly and takes F12 and --screenshot-frame
+        // (the port's regression instrument) with it.
+        static std::vector<uint8_t> scratch;
+        const size_t npx = (size_t)width * (size_t)height;
+        scratch.resize(npx * 4);
+        glReadPixels(x, y, width, height, GL_RGBA, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, scratch.data());
+        ok = (glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR);
+        if (ok) {
+            const uint8_t *src = scratch.data();
+            uint8_t *dst = (uint8_t *)rgb;
+            for (size_t i = 0; i < npx; ++i, src += 4, dst += 3) {
+                dst[0] = src[0];
+                dst[1] = src[1];
+                dst[2] = src[2];
+            }
+        }
+    } else {
+        glReadPixels(x, y, width, height, GL_RGB, GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE, rgb);
+        ok = (glGetError() == GL_NO_ERROR);
+    }
 
     glPixelStorei(GL_PACK_ALIGNMENT, prevalign);
     glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, framebuffers[current_framebuffer].fbo);
